Changelog: 05-11-2026 02:36:25

Added. SSD Check: the health, power cycles and power-on hours of each drive that reports SMART, read from udisks
over D-Bus without root (busctl). An NVMe drive gives all three (health is 100 minus its percentage used); a SATA SSD
gives its hours and cycles and its health from the first known maker's attribute (231, 169, 202, 233, 177), else
"Not reported". The state beside the name shows a problem the drive itself flags; with more drives a list chooses
one. The drive's serial number stays out of the window. Written by tools/new_app.py from the architecture chapter.
